>  Mike Piff

I think that you are misusing the th environment.  In LaTeX 2.09 I
find that actually having a theorem before the nested list solves the
problem.  Perhaps something could be done to newtheorem to alert naive
users to this kind of abuse.



                                        -paul




\documentstyle[12pt]{article} \newtheorem{th}{Theorem}
\begin{document}
\begin{enumerate}
   \item
   \begin{enumerate}
      \item  This looks
      \item  good
   \end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}
\begin{th} foo
   \begin{enumerate}
      \item $\leftarrow$This space is too big
      \item
   \end{enumerate}
\end{th}
